   "path": "SCENE.md",
   "role": "instructions",
   "content": "# Variable Font Morph\n\nSweeps a variable font's weight and width axes across a line, one character at a time, so the type swells and slims in a wave.\n\nCategory: typography. Length: 5 s. WebGL: no.\n\nUse when:\n- Display type should breathe: weight and width swelling in a travelling wave.\n- A kinetic title with a variable font where the letterforms themselves are the motion.\n\nAvoid when:\n- The type must hold one fixed style.\n- You want letters to move position: use wave-text.\n\nVariables:\n- text (string): Text, default \"Stretch and\\nbreathe\"\n- font_size (number, 24-260): Font size, default 130\n- color (color): Color, default \"#f4f4f5\"\n- mode (enum): Split by, default \"chars\"\n- order (enum): Order, default \"start\"\n- stagger_frames (number, 0-20): Stagger, default 3\n- duration_frames (number, 1-90): Unit duration, default 24\n- delay_frames (number, 0-120): Delay, default 6\n- exit (boolean): Exit, default false\n- weight_from (number, 100-900): Weight from, default 200\n- weight_to (number, 100-900): Weight to, default 900\n- width_from (number, 50-150): Width from, default 60\n- width_to (number, 50-150): Width to, default 125\n- oscillate (boolean): Oscillate, default true\n- period_frames (number, 12-240): Period, default 60\n- phase_step (number, 0-3): Phase step, default 0.55\n- reserve_space (boolean): Reserve space, default true\n\nSource: https://github.com/riaz37/remotion-ui. Licence: MIT. The scene file keeps the upstream notice.\n"
  },
  {
   "path": "scene.html",
   "role": "source",
   "content": "<!doctype html>\n<!--\n  Variable Font Morph\n\n  Sweeps a variable font's weight and width axes across a line, one character at a time, so the type swells and slims in a wave.\n\n  Ported to an HTML + GSAP sub-composition by usemosio/blocks from:\n  https://github.com/riaz37/remotion-ui/blob/0aecaca2b61a167992e1205d10e4da16d8a71331/apps/web/registry/bases/default/primitives/variable-font-morph.tsx\n\n  MIT License\n\n  Copyright (c) 2026 RemotionUI\n\n  Permission is hereby granted, free of charge, to any person obtaining a copy\n  of this software and associated documentation files (the \"Software\"), to deal\n  in the Software without restriction, including without limitation the rights\n  to use, copy, modify, merge, publish, distribute, sublicense, and/or sell\n  copies of the Software, and to permit persons to whom the Software is\n  furnished to do so, subject to the following conditions:\n\n  The above copyright notice and this permission notice shall be included in all\n  copies or substantial portions of the Software.\n\n  THE SOFTWARE IS PROVIDED \"AS IS\", WITHOUT WARRANTY OF ANY KIND, EXPRESS OR\n  IMPLIED, INCLUDING BUT NOT LIMITED TO THE WARRANTIES OF MERCHANTABILITY,\n  FITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR PURPOSE AND NONINFRINGEMENT. IN NO EVENT SHALL THE\n  AUTHORS OR COPYRIGHT HOLDERS BE LIABLE FOR ANY CLAIM, DAMAGES OR OTHER\n  LIABILITY, WHETHER IN AN ACTION OF CONTRACT, TORT OR OTHERWISE, ARISING FROM,\n  OUT OF OR IN CONNECTION WITH THE SOFTWARE OR THE USE OR OTHER DEALINGS IN THE\n  SOFTWARE.\n-->\n<html\n  lang=\"en\"\n  data-composition-id=\"variable-font-morph\"\n  data-composition-duration=\"5\"\n  data-composition-variables='[\n    [\n      {\n        \"id\": \"text\",\n        \"type\": \"string\",\n        \"role\": \"content\",\n        \"label\": \"Text\",\n        \"description\": \"The text. A line break starts a new line.\",\n        \"default\": \"Stretch and\\nbreathe\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"font_size\",\n        \"type\": \"number\",\n        \"role\": \"style\",\n        \"label\": \"Font size\",\n        \"description\": \"Text size in pixels.\",\n        \"default\": 130,\n        \"min\": 24,\n        \"max\": 260,\n        \"step\": 1,\n        \"unit\": \"px\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"color\",\n        \"type\": \"color\",\n        \"role\": \"style\",\n        \"label\": \"Color\",\n        \"description\": \"Text color.\",\n        \"default\": \"#f4f4f5\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"mode\",\n        \"type\": \"enum\",\n        \"role\": \"motion\",\n        \"label\": \"Split by\",\n        \"description\": \"What one animated unit is.\",\n        \"default\": \"chars\",\n        \"options\": [\n          {\n            \"value\": \"chars\",\n            \"label\": \"Characters\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"value\": \"words\",\n            \"label\": \"Words\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"value\": \"lines\",\n            \"label\": \"Lines\"\n          }\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"order\",\n        \"type\": \"enum\",\n        \"role\": \"motion\",\n        \"label\": \"Order\",\n        \"description\": \"Order the units arrive in.\",\n        \"default\": \"start\",\n        \"options\": [\n          {\n            \"value\": \"start\",\n            \"label\": \"Start to end\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"value\": \"end\",\n            \"label\": \"End to start\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"value\": \"center\",\n            \"label\": \"Centre outwards\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"value\": \"edges\",\n            \"label\": \"Edges inwards\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"value\": \"random\",\n            \"label\": \"Random\"\n          }\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"stagger_frames\",\n        \"type\": \"number\",\n        \"role\": \"motion\",\n        \"label\": \"Stagger\",\n        \"description\": \"Frames (30 per second) between one unit and the next.\",\n        \"default\": 3,\n        \"min\": 0,\n        \"max\": 20,\n        \"step\": 1,\n        \"unit\": \"frames\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"duration_frames\",\n        \"type\": \"number\",\n        \"role\": \"motion\",\n        \"label\": \"Unit duration\",\n        \"description\": \"Frames one unit takes to arrive.\",\n        \"default\": 24,\n        \"min\": 1,\n        \"max\": 90,\n        \"step\": 1,\n        \"unit\": \"frames\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"delay_frames\",\n        \"type\": \"number\",\n        \"role\": \"motion\",\n        \"label\": \"Delay\",\n        \"description\": \"Frames before the first unit starts.\",\n        \"default\": 6,\n        \"min\": 0,\n        \"max\": 120,\n        \"step\": 1,\n        \"unit\": \"frames\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"exit\",\n        \"type\": \"boolean\",\n        \"role\": \"motion\",\n        \"label\": \"Exit\",\n        \"description\": \"Play an exit at the end of the clip.\",\n        \"default\": false\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"weight_from\",\n        \"type\": \"number\",\n        \"role\": \"style\",\n        \"label\": \"Weight from\",\n        \"description\": \"Weight axis at the start of the sweep (100 to 900).\",\n        \"default\": 200,\n        \"min\": 100,\n        \"max\": 900,\n        \"step\": 10\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"weight_to\",\n        \"type\": \"number\",\n        \"role\": \"style\",\n        \"label\": \"Weight to\",\n        \"description\": \"Weight axis at the end of the sweep.\",\n        \"default\": 900,\n        \"min\": 100,\n        \"max\": 900,\n        \"step\": 10\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"width_from\",\n        \"type\": \"number\",\n        \"role\": \"style\",\n        \"label\": \"Width from\",\n        \"description\": \"Width axis at the start of the sweep (50 to 150).\",\n        \"default\": 60,\n        \"min\": 50,\n        \"max\": 150,\n        \"step\": 1,\n        \"unit\": \"%\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"width_to\",\n        \"type\": \"number\",\n        \"role\": \"style\",\n        \"label\": \"Width to\",\n        \"description\": \"Width axis at the end of the sweep.\",\n        \"default\": 125,\n        \"min\": 50,\n        \"max\": 150,\n        \"step\": 1,\n        \"unit\": \"%\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"oscillate\",\n        \"type\": \"boolean\",\n        \"role\": \"motion\",\n        \"label\": \"Oscillate\",\n        \"description\": \"Keep the axes swinging after the entrance instead of settling on the heavy end.\",\n        \"default\": true\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"period_frames\",\n        \"type\": \"number\",\n        \"role\": \"motion\",\n        \"label\": \"Period\",\n        \"description\": \"Frames (30 per second) for one full swing.\",\n        \"default\": 60,\n        \"min\": 12,\n        \"max\": 240,\n        \"step\": 1,\n        \"unit\": \"frames\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"phase_step\",\n        \"type\": \"number\",\n        \"role\": \"motion\",\n        \"label\": \"Phase step\",\n        \"description\": \"Phase offset between neighbouring characters, in radians.\",\n        \"default\": 0.55,\n        \"min\": 0,\n        \"max\": 3,\n        \"step\": 0.05\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"reserve_space\",\n        \"type\": \"boolean\",\n        \"role\": \"style\",\n        \"label\": \"Reserve space\",\n        \"description\": \"Hold each character&#39;s widest width so the line does not reflow while it morphs.\",\n        \"default\": true\n      }\n    ]\n  ]'\n>\n  <head>\n    <meta charset=\"UTF-8\" />\n    <title>Variable Font Morph</title>\n  </head>\n  <body>\n    <template>\n      <link\n        rel=\"stylesheet\"\n        href=\"https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Anybody:wdth,wght@50..150,100..900&amp;display=block\"\n      />\n      <style>\n        #root {\n          position: absolute;\n          inset: 0;\n          overflow: hidden;\n          container-type: size;\n          pointer-events: none;\n        }\n        #root { color: #f4f4f5; }\n        .vfm-stage { position: absolute; inset: 0; display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; }\n        .vfm-text { display: inline-flex; flex-direction: column; align-items: center; text-align: center; max-width: 90%; line-height: 1.15; }\n        .vfm-line { display: block; white-space: normal; }\n        .vfm-word { display: inline-block; white-space: nowrap; }\n        .vfm-unit { display: inline-block; white-space: pre; }\n        .vfm-unit { display: inline-grid; }\n        .vfm-ghost { grid-area: 1 / 1; visibility: hidden; }\n        .vfm-glyph { grid-area: 1 / 1; justify-self: center; }\n      </style>\n\n      <div id=\"root\" data-composition-id=\"variable-font-morph\" data-duration=\"5\" data-fps=\"30\">\n        <div id=\"vfm-clip\" class=\"vfm-stage clip\" data-start=\"0\" data-duration=\"5\" data-track-index=\"0\">\n          <span id=\"vfm-text\" class=\"vfm-text\" role=\"img\"></span>\n        </div>\n\n        <script src=\"https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/gsap@3.14.2/dist/gsap.min.js\"></script>\n        <script>\n          (function () {\n            \"use strict\";\n            var root = document.getElementById(\"root\");\n            var vars = window.__hyperframes && window.__hyperframes.getVariables ? window.__hyperframes.getVariables() : {};\n            function num(v, f, min, max) { var n = Number(v); return Number.isFinite(n) && v !== \"\" && v !== null ? Math.min(max, Math.max(min, n)) : f; }\n            function str(v, f) { return typeof v === \"string\" && v.trim() ? v : f; }\n            function bool(v, f) { if (v === undefined || v === null || v === \"\") return f; return !(v === false || v === \"false\" || v === 0 || v === \"0\"); }\n            function pick(v, list, f) { v = String(v); return list.indexOf(v) >= 0 ? v : f; }\n            function clamp01(v) { return v < 0 ? 0 : v > 1 ? 1 : v; }\n            function lerp(a, b, t) { return a + (b - a) * t; }\n            function ramp(v, a, b, from, to, ease) { var p = b === a ? 1 : clamp01((v - a) / (b - a)); if (ease) p = ease(p); return from + (to - from) * p; }\n            function bez(x1, y1, x2, y2) {\n              return function (x) {\n                if (x <= 0) return 0;\n                if (x >= 1) return 1;\n                var lo = 0, hi = 1, t = x;\n                for (var i = 0; i < 30; i++) {\n                  var cx = 3 * (1 - t) * (1 - t) * t * x1 + 3 * (1 - t) * t * t * x2 + t * t * t;\n                  if (cx < x) lo = t; else hi = t;\n                  t = (lo + hi) / 2;\n                }\n                return 3 * (1 - t) * (1 - t) * t * y1 + 3 * (1 - t) * t * t * y2 + t * t * t;\n              };\n            }\n            function mulberry32(a) { return function () { a |= 0; a = (a + 0x6d2b79f5) | 0; var t = Math.imul(a ^ (a >>> 15), 1 | a); t = (t + Math.imul(t ^ (t >>> 7), 61 | t)) ^ t; return ((t ^ (t >>> 14)) >>> 0) / 4294967296; }; }\n            function mk(tag, parent, cls, text) { var e = document.createElement(tag); if (cls) e.className = cls; if (text !== undefined) e.textContent = text; if (parent) parent.appendChild(e); return e; }\n            var TOTAL = parseFloat(root.dataset.duration || \"5\");\n            // Every frame is drawn from the frame number alone, so seeking anywhere draws the same frame.\n            function drive(name, frameFn) {\n              var clock = { f: 0 };\n              var tl = gsap.timeline({ paused: true });\n              tl.to(clock, { f: TOTAL * 30, duration: TOTAL, ease: \"none\", onUpdate: function () { frameFn(clock.f); } }, 0);\n              frameFn(0);\n              tl.seek(0);\n              window.__timelines = window.__timelines || {};\n              window.__timelines[name] = tl;\n            }\n\n            // ---- Split text into lines, words and units (characters, words or lines), staggered like the source library's useSplitText ----\n            var ENTER = bez(0.16, 1, 0.3, 1);\n            function EXIT(t) { return t * t * t; }\n            function splitText(text, mode) {\n              var lines = [], units = [];\n              String(text).split(/\\r?\\n/).forEach(function (raw) {\n                var words = [];\n                var rawWords = mode === \"lines\" ? [raw.trim()].filter(Boolean) : raw.split(/\\s+/).filter(Boolean);\n                rawWords.forEach(function (w) {\n                  var pieces = mode === \"chars\" ? Array.from(w) : [w];\n                  var us = pieces.map(function (p) { var u = { text: p, index: units.length }; units.push(u); return u; });\n                  words.push({ units: us });\n                });\n                lines.push({ words: words });\n              });\n              return { lines: lines, units: units };\n            }\n            function staggerRanks(total, order, seed) {\n              var idx = [], i, mid = (total - 1) / 2;\n              for (i = 0; i < total; i++) idx.push(i);\n              if (order === \"end\") return idx.map(function (k) { return total - 1 - k; });\n              if (order === \"center\") return idx.map(function (k) { return Math.round(Math.abs(k - mid)); });\n              if (order === \"edges\") return idx.map(function (k) { return Math.round(mid - Math.abs(k - mid)); });\n              if (order === \"random\") {\n                var rng = mulberry32(seed || 1), keys = idx.map(function () { return rng(); });\n                var sorted = idx.slice().sort(function (a, b) { return keys[a] - keys[b]; });\n                var out = new Array(total);\n                sorted.forEach(function (orig, rank) { out[orig] = rank; });\n                return out;\n              }\n              return idx;\n            }\n            // o: stagger, duration, delay (frames), order, seed, exit (bool), exitFrames\n            function makeTiming(split, o) {\n              var rk = staggerRanks(split.units.length, o.order, o.seed);\n              var maxRank = rk.length ? Math.max.apply(null, rk) : 0;\n              var lastEnter = o.delay + maxRank * o.stagger + o.duration;\n              var exitFrames = Math.max(1, Math.round(o.exitFrames || Math.max(6, Math.round(o.duration * 0.7))));\n              var exitStart = null;\n              if (o.exit) exitStart = Math.max(TOTAL * 30 - exitFrames - maxRank * o.stagger, lastEnter);\n              return { ranks: rk, o: o, exitFrames: exitFrames, exitStart: exitStart, lastEnter: lastEnter };\n            }\n            function unitState(frame, T, u) {\n              var rank = T.ranks[u.index], o = T.o;\n              var start = o.delay + rank * o.stagger;\n              var et = clamp01((frame - start) / o.duration);\n              var enter = ENTER(et), eo = clamp01(et / 0.55);\n              if (T.exitStart === null) return { enter: enter, exit: 0, displace: 1 - enter, opacity: eo, value: enter };\n              var us = T.exitStart + rank * o.stagger;\n              var xt = clamp01((frame - us) / T.exitFrames);\n              var ex = EXIT(xt), xo = 1 - clamp01(xt / 0.7);\n              return { enter: enter, exit: ex, displace: ex > 0 ? ex : 1 - enter, opacity: eo * xo, value: enter * (1 - ex) };\n            }\n            // Builds lines > words > unit spans into parent. fill(unitEl, u) fills each unit.\n            function buildSplit(parent, split, pre, wordGap, fill) {\n              split.lines.forEach(function (line) {\n                var lineEl = mk(\"span\", parent, pre + \"-line\");\n                line.words.forEach(function (word, wi) {\n                  var wordEl = mk(\"span\", lineEl, pre + \"-word\");\n                  if (wi < line.words.length - 1) wordEl.style.marginRight = wordGap + \"em\";\n                  word.units.forEach(function (u) {\n                    u.el = mk(\"span\", wordEl, pre + \"-unit\");\n                    fill(u.el, u);\n                  });\n                });\n              });\n            }\n            function splitCss(pre) {\n              return \".\" + pre + \"-text { display: inline-flex; flex-direction: column; align-items: center; text-align: center; max-width: 90%; line-height: 1.15; }\\n\" +\n                \".\" + pre + \"-line { display: block; white-space: normal; }\\n\" +\n                \".\" + pre + \"-word { display: inline-block; }\\n\" +\n                \".\" + pre + \"-unit { display: inline-block; white-space: pre; }\\n\";\n            }\n\n            var DEFAULT_TEXT = \"Stretch and\\nbreathe\", DEF_STAGGER = 3, DEF_DURATION = 24, DEF_EXIT = false;\n            root.style.fontFamily = \"Anybody, system-ui, sans-serif\";\n\n            var text = str(vars.text, DEFAULT_TEXT);\n            var mode = pick(vars.mode, [\"chars\", \"words\", \"lines\"], \"chars\");\n            var MODE_STAGGER = { chars: 2, words: 4, lines: 7 };\n            var split = splitText(text, mode);\n            var T = makeTiming(split, {\n              stagger: num(vars.stagger_frames, DEF_STAGGER, 0, 20), duration: num(vars.duration_frames, DEF_DURATION, 1, 90), delay: num(vars.delay_frames, 6, 0, 120),\n              order: pick(vars.order, [\"start\", \"end\", \"center\", \"edges\", \"random\"], \"start\"), seed: 1, exit: bool(vars.exit, DEF_EXIT)\n            });\n\n            var textEl = document.getElementById(\"vfm-text\");\n            textEl.style.fontSize = num(vars.font_size, 130, 24, 260) + \"px\";\n            textEl.style.fontWeight = \"400\";\n            textEl.style.color = str(vars.color, \"#f4f4f5\");\n            textEl.setAttribute(\"aria-label\", text);\n\n            var w0 = num(vars.weight_from, 200, 100, 900), w1 = num(vars.weight_to, 900, 100, 900);\n            var d0 = num(vars.width_from, 60, 50, 150), d1 = num(vars.width_to, 125, 50, 150);\n            var oscillate = bool(vars.oscillate, true), period = num(vars.period_frames, 60, 12, 240), phaseStep = num(vars.phase_step, 0.55, 0, 3), reserve = bool(vars.reserve_space, true);\n            var heaviest = Math.max(w0, w1), widest = Math.max(d0, d1);\n            buildSplit(textEl, split, \"vfm\", 0.26, function (el, u) {\n              if (reserve) {\n                var g = mk(\"span\", el, \"vfm-ghost\", u.text);\n                g.setAttribute(\"aria-hidden\", \"true\");\n                g.style.fontVariationSettings = '\"wght\" ' + heaviest + ', \"wdth\" ' + widest;\n              }\n              u.glyph = mk(\"span\", el, reserve ? \"vfm-glyph\" : \"\", u.text);\n            });\n            function draw(frame) {\n              split.units.forEach(function (u) {\n                var s = unitState(frame, T, u);\n                var wave = oscillate ? 0.5 + 0.5 * Math.sin((frame / period) * Math.PI * 2 - u.index * phaseStep) : 1;\n                var pos = clamp01(s.enter) * wave * (1 - s.exit);\n                u.glyph.style.opacity = String(s.opacity);\n                u.glyph.style.fontVariationSettings = '\"wght\" ' + lerp(w0, w1, pos).toFixed(1) + ', \"wdth\" ' + lerp(d0, d1, pos).toFixed(1);\n              });\n            }\n            drive(\"variable-font-morph\", draw);\n          })();\n        </script>\n      </div>\n    </template>\n  </body>\n</html>\n"
  }
 ],
